								{
									"text": "I created `pipelines/invoice-fields.pipe`. It validates with no errors or warnings, but I haven't run it on an invoice, so the extraction itself is untested.\n\n**How it works**\n1. `webhook` receives the invoice file.\n2. `parse` turns the PDF or plain text into text.\n3. `extract_data` asks OpenAI (`llm_openai`, profile `openai-5-4-mini`) for four fields:\n   - `invoice_number` as text\n   - `vendor` as text\n   - `total` as a decimal number\n   - `due_date` as a date\n4. `response_answers` returns those fields as the webhook response.\n\n**What you need to do:** add a Variable named `ROCKETRIDE_OPENAI_KEY` holding your OpenAI key. The pipeline reads it only through that placeholder. I couldn't check whether it already exists, because the key-listing call isn't available in this environment.\n\n**Not tested:** I started the pipeline with `use`. I couldn't send a file to it or read its status, because the task token is redacted in my tools. I don't know whether `total` and `due_date` come back typed as a number and a date. I also haven't checked that a missing field returns an empty value.\n\nTo change the model, edit the profile name in `llm_openai_1`. For example, `openai-5-4` is the larger model.",
									"type": "text"
								}
